# Generated and reference material, kept on disk but out of the history.
#
# Both were committed and both are large. graphify-out is the graph tool's output -
# regenerated on demand, so a copy in git is a copy that goes stale. reference_docs is
# 270MB of sample certificates, and is most of why .git is 285MB.
#
# Untracking them stops the history growing further. It does not shrink what is already
# there: those files stay in every past commit, and removing them from history means
# rewriting it - which changes every commit id and breaks every existing clone. That is
# a decision to take deliberately, not a side effect of tidying.
graphify-out/
apps/web-hta/reference_docs/
